  "title": "Ph Life Insurance Handbook — 5. Supplemental Riders (Add-On Benefits)",
  "content": "## 5. Supplemental Riders (Add-On Benefits)\nPolicyholders can attach optional riders to enhance coverage:\n1. **Accidental Death and Dismemberment (ADB)**:\n   - Doubles the face payout if death occurs as a direct result of an accident.\n   - Pays schedule of indemnities for loss of limbs, sight, or hearing.\n2. **Critical Illness Benefit (CIB)**:\n   - Lump-sum cash payout upon diagnosis of any of 36 covered critical illnesses (including stroke, cancer, heart attack, kidney failure, major organ transplant).\n   - Additional rider premium starting at ₱450/month for ₱500,000 critical illness coverage.\n3. **Waiver of Premium upon Disability (WP)**:\n   - Waives all future policy premiums if the insured becomes totally and permanently disabled before age 60, while keeping the full death benefit active.\n4. **Hospital Income Rider (HIR)**:\n   - Daily cash allowance (₱1,000 to ₱5,000 per day) during hospital confinement for injury or sickness.\n\n---",
